	(text "CHANNELS 1-4"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 55.88 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "171e3dae-5485-5ab3-b722-9353643ce7d7")
	)
	(text "TSB582 DECOUPLING"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 106.68 251.46 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "17ff4d06-33f9-5b9d-b5f8-f6aed7c5950f")
	)
	(text "OUTPUT SWITCH DECOUPLING"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 327.66 193.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1a5b14c2-1614-5f17-a250-b9dc2abde610")
	)
	(text "At 100 mA the pin sits about 1.5 V under the rail (0.55 V typ in the op amp, about 1 V in the 8-11 ohm switch). The ADC reads every pin, so firmware can check it. Channels 1 and 2 take their level from the GPIO gate on their own sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 27 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "24064432-4ae9-52a0-8eab-db2310f95afd")
	)
	(text "BIAS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 236.22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4718eeb0-d879-54a1-83f4-ed89853846be")
	)
	(text "Open, the switch leaves only leakage on the pin. It also opens by itself when the pin is forced above +12V or below ground (FF goes low), so an outside source cannot feed the 12 V rail. Up to 100 mA per output: the switch rating (the op amp gives 150 mA min)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 21 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4a1016e2-cf06-5c3a-9e17-e36fde96c6b3")
	)
	(text "Output drivers: each TSB582 section multiplies its channel level by 1 + 191k / 49.9k = 4.83 (0-12 V from +12V). A TMUX7412F section joins it to the pin while OUT_EN is high. Feedback is taken ahead of the switch."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.8 1.8)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ba719860-1d6c-5a13-960e-38adb3d11815")
	)
